.DS_Store

# ds-bundle/ is intentionally NOT ignored. There is no converter script that
# regenerates it — the extracted CSS and the per-component docs are authored
# content, so losing them would mean redoing real work.

# Xcode
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# Build output. Both spellings matter and only one of them is obvious: SwiftPM
# writes .build/, but xcodebuild writes build/ whenever it is handed a SYMROOT
# or a -derivedDataPath inside the repo, and that is how 658 object files and
# precompiled modules — 73 MB, some of them recording the absolute path of
# whichever worktree produced them — were once committed here. Nothing in the
# tree depends on either directory; both regenerate from a clean checkout.
.build/
build/

# Signing material and anything carrying a secret. None of it has been
# committed; these rules exist so it cannot start.
*.p12
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
.env
.env.*

# Distribution artefacts, for the same reason as build output.
*.ipa
*.xcarchive
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip

# SwiftPM local state. Package.resolved is deliberately absent from this list —
# there are no external dependencies to pin, and if that ever changes the
# resolved versions should be tracked, not ignored.
.swiftpm/
